{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Finprod","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_bonds_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_bonds_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L113-L118","doc":"With every interface scalar zero the product collapses to `X ^ n` -- the\nbare-word composition law `G_A = x^(A-1) · G_1^A` measured in\n`body_order_composition_probe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_bonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_bonds","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L102-L111","doc":"Applying a list of interfaces with scalars `ds` multiplies by the product\n`∏ (X + C d)`. Induction on the list; this is the composition across `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_interface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_interface","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L93-L100","doc":"**The canonical interface is multiplication by `X + C d`.**\n\nThe interface `σ_g + d·I` acts as (promotion) + (`d` times the original), and\nthe generating function turns that into `(X + C d) · G`. With `d = 0` it\ndegenerates to `gf_shift`, which is the bare-word bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_shift","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**A degree shift is multiplication by `X`.**\n\nThis is the promotion theorem's image in the generating function: raising every\ndegree by one, with coefficients untouched, multiplies `G` by `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_pi","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L63-L81","doc":"**Multiplicativity over a dependent product index set.**\n\nWhen the index set is `∏ᵢ S i`, the coefficient multiplicative across factors\nand the degree additive, the generating function is the product of the factors'\ngenerating functions.\n\nThis is the form the block factorisation needs: nucleon blocks are *not*\nidentical to one another -- block `i` is supported on strands `[bᵢ, bᵢ₊₁)` --\nso the family `S i` must be allowed to vary with `i`. The constant-family case\nis `QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.gf_pow`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_congr","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L56-L61","doc":"**Congruence in the degree**: only degrees at indices actually present in\n`s` can matter. Used to replace a per-block degree sum by the length of the\nassembled word, which agree only on the product index set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_empty","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L53-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction.gf","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/GradedGeneratingFunction.lean#L46-L51","doc":"The grade generating function `∑_{i ∈ s} c i · X^(deg i)`.\n\nOver `ℤ[q,q⁻¹]` with `deg` the Coxeter length and `c` the normal-form\ncoefficients, this is the `G_E(x)` the arc measures. ","signatureChunk":0}]}